# your-spotify — Secrets (placeholder, no real values)

spotifySecretFile expects a path to a file containing your Spotify Developer app's client secret — e.g. `/run/secrets/your-spotify-client-secret` if you're using a secrets manager (sops-nix, agenix, etc.), or a plain file with restricted permissions if not. Do not put the actual secret value directly in module.nix or config.nix — those get committed to your repo. Get spotifyPublic (client ID) and the secret by registering an app at Spotify's developer dashboard.

Never commit an actual secret value into this file or into module.nix/config.nix.
This file exists to document *what* is needed and *where* it should come from, not
to hold the secret itself.
